00:42:30,000 --> 00:42:36,000
The Dancer (French: La Danseuse) is a 2016 biographical historical drama film about dancer Loie Fuller, directed by Stéphanie Di Giusto from a
screenplay she co-wrote with Sarah Thiebaud and Thomas Bidegain, based on the novel Loïe Fuller: Danseuse de la Belle Époque by Giovanni Lista.

7
00:49:35,000 --> 00:49:41,000
The film stars Soko, Gaspard Ulliel, Mélanie Thierry, Lily-Rose Depp,
François Damiens, Louis-Do de Lencquesaing and Denis Ménochet.

8
00:56:40,000 --> 00:56:46,000
The film is a co-production between France, Belgium and Czech Republic.

9
01:03:45,000 --> 01:03:51,000
The film made its world premiere in the Un Certain Regard
section of the 2016 Cannes Film Festival.

10
01:10:50,000 --> 01:10:56,000
It was released theatrically on 28 September 2016 in France by Wild Bunch and in Belgium by
Lumière, and on 19 January 2017 in the Czech Republic by Film Distribution Artcam.

11
01:17:55,000 --> 01:18:01,000
The film explores themes of dance, ballet dancer, ballet.
